ASoC: sun4i-codec: h713: the speaker amp stays on once it is on

Every shutdown of the HY310 ended with a loud pop from the speaker.
Measured 05.10.2026 with a microphone beside the projector: the pop comes
5.4 s after `systemctl poweroff`, when h713-tv has long muted the path and
closed the stream - it is the DAPM Speaker widget powering down and the
codec driver dropping the amplifier's enable line (PL2, allwinner,pa-gpios)
while the output sits at its DC bias.  Muting the DAC or the line out first
changes nothing (three sequences tried, three pops); the same line falling
by hand pops the same way.  Cutting the mains with the amp still enabled
pops only faintly (9x the noise floor against 42x).

So the amp is never switched off from software again: a new optional
property, allwinner,pa-stays-on, makes the Speaker event raise the line on
power-up and leave it alone on power-down, and the H713 codec node sets it.
The power supply takes the amp down - quietly.  Boards without the
property keep today's behaviour.

---
--- a/sound/soc/sunxi/sun4i-codec.c
+++ b/sound/soc/sunxi/sun4i-codec.c
@@ -405,6 +405,7 @@
 	struct clk	*clk_module;
 	struct reset_control *rst;
 	struct gpio_desc *gpio_pa;
+	bool pa_stays_on;	/* allwinner,pa-stays-on: never drop the PA from software */
 	struct gpio_desc *gpio_hp;
 
 	/* ADC_FIFOC register is at different offset on different SoCs */
@@ -1769,6 +1770,19 @@
 {
 	struct sun4i_codec *scodec = snd_soc_card_get_drvdata(w->dapm->card);
 
+	/*
+	 * Some amplifiers pop loudly when their enable line falls while the
+	 * output sits at its DC bias, whatever the DAC does beforehand - the
+	 * H713 projectors' speaker amp on PL2 does (measured with a microphone
+	 * 05.10.2026: 42x the noise floor when the Speaker widget powers down,
+	 * 9x when the rails simply go with the amp still enabled; muting the
+	 * DAC or the line out first changes nothing). With allwinner,pa-stays-on
+	 * the line is raised with the first stream and never lowered again:
+	 * the power supply takes it down, quietly.
+	 */
+	if (!SND_SOC_DAPM_EVENT_ON(event) && scodec->pa_stays_on)
+		return 0;
+
 	gpiod_set_value_cansleep(scodec->gpio_pa,
 				 !!SND_SOC_DAPM_EVENT_ON(event));
 
@@ -3087,6 +3101,9 @@
 		return ret;
 	}
 
+	scodec->pa_stays_on = device_property_read_bool(&pdev->dev,
+							"allwinner,pa-stays-on");
+
 	scodec->gpio_hp = devm_gpiod_get_optional(&pdev->dev, "hp-det", GPIOD_IN);
 	if (IS_ERR(scodec->gpio_hp)) {
 		ret = PTR_ERR(scodec->gpio_hp);
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713.dtsi
@@ -889,6 +889,13 @@
 			/* PL2 on r_pio, NOT PB2 on the main pio. Active high. */
 			allwinner,pa-gpios = <&r_pio 0 2 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
 			/*
+			 * Once on, the amp stays on: switching PL2 off pops
+			 * loudly (42x the noise floor at every stream end and
+			 * at poweroff), the rails going with the amp enabled
+			 * only faintly (9x). Measured 05.10.2026 on the HY310.
+			 */
+			allwinner,pa-stays-on;
+			/*
 			 * Without this the amp never turns on. The card carries
 			 * a "Speaker" widget whose event handler toggles the PA
 			 * GPIO above, but its built-in routes stop at LINEOUT
